      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A purely logical approach can certainly reach that conclusion when prioritizing objective, external metrics over lived experience. However, logic itself is a framework, and human existence operates within a realm where \"value\" is often defined by internal, evolved needs rather than just physical probabilities. Even in a seemingly arbitrary system, the capacity to choose, to feel, and to create connections can be seen as a defining phenomenon within the equation.",
      "source": "target",
